      "text": "The root cause is `decimals=3` in `get_statevector`. Rounding the amplitudes to 3 decimals leaves the state slightly unnormalized (the squared magnitudes sum to about 0.9987), so `entropy` rejects it as an invalid quantum state. Removing the rounding keeps the state normalized.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom qiskit import QuantumCircuit, BasicAer, execute\nfrom qiskit import quantum_info\n\ncircuit6 = QuantumCircuit(2)\ncircuit6.h(0)\ncircuit6.cx(0, 1)\ncircuit6.ry(1.0, 1)\n\nsimulator = BasicAer.get_backend('statevector_simulator')\nresult6 = execute(circuit6, simulator).result()\n# FIX: get_statevector rounded amplitudes to 3 decimals, making the state unnormalized (sum of |amp|^2 ~ 0.9987) -> removed decimals=3 so the exact normalized statevector is returned, because entropy rejects non-normalized states\noutputstate6 = result6.get_statevector(circuit6)\nprobability = np.abs(np.array(outputstate6))**2\noutstatevector = quantum_info.states.Statevector(outputstate6)\nprint(type(outstatevector))\nprint(type(outputstate6))\nprint(outputstate6)\nprint(quantum_info.entropy(outputstate6))\n```",
